#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Gives the Road journal two plain download links (A4 first, US Letter second) through the same confirm step, with nothing counted, and tests that protect Gill's decisions. The new test is only put in place if every edit succeeds. The PDFs are NOT in this package: copy them in first.

Run it from the project folder, AFTER unzipping starscapes-road-journal-links-23oct.zip into it:   python3 tools/add-road-journal-links.py

What it does: it makes exact edits to 7 files and, only if all succeed, puts one new test in place.
  lib/newsletterAdmin.js, src/explorers/RoadJournalPage.jsx, src/explorers/explorersConfig.js, src/newsletter/NewsletterLinkPage.jsx, src/newsletter/newsletter.css, src/newsletter/newsletterRules.js, test/explorers-bay-requests.test.js

How it keeps you safe:
  - It checks ALL 7 files first. If any is not exactly the way it expects, it changes NOTHING and says which.
  - Before changing a file it keeps a copy, ending .before-road-journal-links.
  - It is safe to run twice: a file already done is left alone.
  - The new files (INSTALL-ROAD-JOURNAL-LINKS.txt, tools/road-journal-links-files/test_road-journal-downloads.test.jsx.staged) come in the zip itself.
"""
